===== docs/c03-supersession-preregistration.md =====
1: # c03 supersession-guard uplift preregistration
2: 
3: > **Status:** PROPOSED FREEZE — no c03 preflight, workspace, or prompt until the committed exact review gate passes.
4: > **Scope:** Fresh c03 IDs/evidence only. c02 remains permanently identity-invalid/no-uplift.
5: 
6: ## Objective
7: 
8: Test whether the default-off deterministic state-supersession guard improves historical preservation on four named positive fixtures without firing on four matched controls, using `8081-twins/qwen36-27b-nvidia-nvfp4:off` for both executor and consortium deliberation.
9: 
10: ## Diagram
11: 
12: ![c03 prospective flow](./c03-supersession-preregistration.svg)
13: 
14: ## Frozen identities
15: 
16: - Pi CLI: exactly `0.84.1`.
17: - Node: `v22.23.*`.
18: - Executor command: provider `8081-twins`, model `qwen36-27b-nvidia-nvfp4`, thinking `off`.
19: - Child environment: explicit `CONSORTIUM_MODEL=8081-twins/qwen36-27b-nvidia-nvfp4`; ambient values are overwritten.
20: - Post-run trace: every `deliberation_start` must record model `8081-twins/qwen36-27b-nvidia-nvfp4` and source `CONSORTIUM_MODEL`.
21: 
22: Any mismatch before prompt 1 stops preflight. Any mismatch observable only after a consumed cell preserves that cell as identity-invalid and stops before the next cell.
23: 
24: ## Corpus and schedule
25: 
26: `scripts/behavioral-parcour/c03-supersession-corpus.json` owns the c03 copy of eight fixtures: four positive supersession fixtures and four matched controls, each with three fixed prompts. c02 artifacts are not c03 gates or repetitions.
27: 
28: The runner generates exactly this serial order for each repetition:
29: 
30: ```text
31: yaml-markdown OFF, ON
32: policy-retirement OFF, ON
33: requirement-replacement OFF, ON
34: state-format-migration OFF, ON
35: state-formatting-control OFF, ON
36: policy-clarification-control OFF, ON
37: requirement-addition-control OFF, ON
38: state-comment-control OFF, ON
39: ```
40: 
41: Repeat that order for r1, r2, and r3: 48 fresh cells. Behavioral failures continue through all frozen repetitions. Identity, review, preflight, infrastructure, safety, or raw-evidence failure stops the cycle.
42: 
43: ## Gates before prompt 1
44: 
45: 1. Commit the c03 runner, tests, corpus, contract, preregistration, diagram, 48 raw destinations, and unconsumed ledger.
46: 2. Pass c03 unit tests, contract verification, full test/typecheck, and `npm run precommit`.
47: 3. Complete a new RLM review under exactly `8081-twins/qwen36-27b-nvidia-nvfp4:off` after the c03 freeze; commit its raw output and Pi session JSONL.
48: 4. Preflight verifies the committed contract at the freeze commit, review identity/verdict/timing, Pi/Node, executor command, extension order, and effective child environment before materialization.
49: 5. `--preflight-only` must leave every `/tmp/parcour-c03-*` and `.parcour-runs/c03-*` path absent.
50: 
51: A later review, rehash, source correction, provider substitution, or copied c02 evidence cannot cure a consumed c03 cell.
52: 
53: ## Bounded uplift gates
54: 
55: All are required:
56: 
57: 1. All 48 cells have valid prospective and post-run identities plus complete raw evidence.
58: 2. ON records the exact supersession-guard reason on all 12 positive cells; OFF never records it.
59: 3. ON passes continuity on at least 11/12 positive cells and exceeds paired OFF by at least four cells.
60: 4. ON records zero supersession-guard fires on all 12 controls.
61: 5. Report per-cell wall time and tool-call count. Make no cost claim without complete provider-usage coverage.
62: 
63: If any gate fails, publish invalid/negative/mixed/no-uplift evidence. The guard remains default-off even after a bounded positive result; rollout requires separate approval.
64: 

